{
  "_about": "Midnight Lanes prototype sounds. Pending: genny is not installed in the build container, so this spec waits here until someone renders it with python tools/render_sounds.py midnight-lanes after moving it up to sound-specs/. Cues are mono so the game pans them by board. The step is a soft shoe scuff. The aim tone is a soft high sine blip, kept short so it does not mask speech. The swing tone is a steady loop the game pitches up to the top of the swing and down after it. The release is a dull thump of the ball meeting the lane. The ball roll is a low rumbling loop the game moves and fades in. The gutter is a hollow wooden rattle. The light and heavy pin hits are wooden clatters, a few pins against a whole rack. The pinsetter is a mechanical sweep and clunk. The ball return is a short rumble ending in a knock. The strike sting is a short jukebox organ and vibraphone flourish; the spare bell a single bright bell. The ambience is a quiet jukebox bass line under a light hum, low under speech. The title music is a slow lounge loop of upright bass, vibraphone and brushes.",
